{"name":"Blueberry Buckle","hex":"#8c99b3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blueberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible round berry, belonging to the cowberry group (Vaccinium sect. Cyanococcus), with flared crowns at the end, that turns blue on ripening.","The shrub of the above-mentioned berry."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark blue colour.","Resembling or characteristic of blueberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blueberry"},{"term":"buckle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metal clasp with a hinged tongue or a spike through which a belt or strap is passed and penetrated by the tongue or spike, in order to fasten the ends of the belt together or to secure the strap to something else.\n\n Some other form of clasp used to fasten two things together.\n\n An image of a clasp (etymology 1, noun sense 1) used as the brisure of an eighth daughter.","Some other form of clasp used to fasten two things together."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten (something) using a buckle (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1); hence , to fasten (something) in any way.","To fasten (something) using a buckle (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1); hence , to fasten (something) in any way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buckle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blueberry","blocks":[{"text":"Blueberries are a widely distributed and widespread group of perennial flowering plants with blue or purple berries. They are classified in the section Cyanococcus within the genus Vaccinium. Commercial blueberries—both wild (lowbush) and cultivated (highbush)—are all native to North America. The highbush varieties were introduced into Europe during the 1930s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Blueberries.jpg/330px-Blueberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blueberry","wikidata":"Q13178"},{"title":"Buckle","blocks":[{"text":"A buckle or clasp is a device used for fastening two loose ends, with one end attached to it and the other held by a catch in a secure but adjustable manner. Often taken for granted, the invention of the buckle was indispensable in securing two ends before the invention of the zipper. The basic buckle frame comes in a variety of shapes and sizes depending on the intended use and fashion of the era. Buckles are as much in use today as they have been in the past: used for much more than just securing one's belt, instead they are one of the most dependable devices in securing a range of items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Soelja.png/330px-Soelja.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckle","wikidata":"Q1135567"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/1280px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blueberries showing various stages of maturation. IG = Immature Green, GP = Green Pink, BP = Blue Pink, and R = Ripe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVaccinium_fruechte_reifestadien.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg/500px-Heidelbeeren_Querschnitt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Heid